  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "The rabbits have more room",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "person-yi-chia-chen-identity-0",
        "person-yi-chia-chen-roster-1"
      ],
      "text": "Yi-Chia Chen leads ARC-AGI-3 at 67.49, with Tufa Labs second at 56.52. Her recorded overnight score improvement from 62.96 increases the distance between them to 10.97 points. The previous evening’s board high was 62.96; against Tufa’s unchanged score, that was a 6.44-point gap. Tonight’s advantage is wider, even though the individual history is too sparse to print a separate net daily change for Chen. The lead is substantial; the contest remains open."
    },
    {
      "heading": "A friendly callback, with tonight’s score",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "person-dries-smit-identity-0",
        "person-dries-smit-roster-1",
        "fact-15486995-3"
      ],
      "text": "The commissioned illustration returns to Chen’s two bunnies and Tufa’s spider mascot, joined by Dries Smit, whose driessmit1 account appears in Tufa’s current roster. Its five spiders and fantastical graphics-card machine are artistic choices, not a team headcount or a report about hardware. The scene follows the friendly sporting humor of Tufa’s October 9 public post; its score chart belongs to tonight’s observed board."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Welcome, PunkCyber’s team",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "social-2109599257980555583",
        "person-punkcyber-identity-0",
        "person-punkcyber-fact-0"
      ],
      "text": "A warm welcome to PunkCyber’s team, 復活の混テキスト. PunkCyber (@cunkpyber) checked in with the Digest today and publicly identified that exact Kaggle name as their team. Its ARC-AGI-3 entry is ninth at 39.53, between NVARC3 in eighth at 40.97 and dreach.ai in tenth at 39.11. An overnight score event records an improvement from 38.15 to 39.53; the prior-evening comparison is unavailable, so that event is not a claimed daily net gain. PunkCyber’s individual Kaggle handle remains unverified, and the reply does not establish who made a submission."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Slayers supplies the big top-ten climb",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "wire-2026-10-12-1003-arc-3-arc-slayer-enters-gold",
        "dispatch-2026-10-12-afternoon-arc3-slayers-and-research",
        "person-keith-tyser-identity-0",
        "person-keith-tyser-roster-2",
        "discussion-arc-3-748593"
      ],
      "text": "ARC Slayers finishes seventh at 41.19, up 9.97 points and from 222nd in the previous-evening comparison. The morning Wire and afternoon dispatch caught the same consequential advance using their own earlier windows. The current roster lists dzjiann, keithtyser and mitubant, including the verified Keith Tyser account. In a public discussion today, dzjiann reports unstable training with Qwen3.8-Flash-Next and slower score progress with Qwen3.8-27B, asking others for advice. That is a participant’s account of experiments, not an established explanation of the team’s new leaderboard result."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Franzen returns near the front",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "wire-2026-10-12-0804-arc-3-daniel-franzen-rushes-into-top-25",
        "wire-2026-10-12-1003-arc-3-jingshui-fu-breaks-into-top-100",
        "person-daniel-franzen-identity-0",
        "person-daniel-franzen-archive-0",
        "person-daniel-franzen-archive-1"
      ],
      "text": "Daniel Franzen is 24th at 35.86. The evening comparison puts him up 3.89 points from 129th; the morning Wire’s much larger climb from 765th describes an earlier rolling window. Franzen was a 2024 champion and 2025 runner-up with the ARChitects. Jingshui Fu’s morning Wire story also deserves its place in the day’s account: it observed Fu 68th at 33.22 after a rise from 3,527th. That is a dated morning observation, rather than a new evening rank or a net-change figure from tonight’s comparison."
    },
    {
      "heading": "The medal line stays tight",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board"
      ],
      "text": "Behind the leading pair, mtg is third at 45.00 and the last dance 🕺 fourth at 43.64. A recorded afternoon event lifted the last dance from 42.55; it is separate from an unavailable net daily comparison. Son & Mark & Ronen holds sixth at 41.97 after a verified 2.73-point gain. Lord Han Solo occupies 18th at 36.98, the public gold cutoff, up from a 36.89 cutoff at the previous close. Public medal bands remain provisional: the private leaderboard settles the finish."
    }
